{"type":"text","timestamp":1794562087126,"sessionID":"ses_e2bc5be0cffe6ETesiCcntOHvn","part":{"id":"prt_1d43c4b9c002WKwBH6KkFc81SQ","sessionID":"ses_e2bc5be0cffe6ETesiCcntOHvn","messageID":"msg_1d43c2a6b001hfteQ5wLcT3n0v","type":"text","text":"T066 is done. Verified.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs` — two edits, comment text unchanged:\n  - Removed the four-line `// A write that throws partway through ... another meaning.` comment from between `].join('\\n');` and the `// 3. ERRORS` banner, leaving exactly one blank line before the banner.\n  - Re-inserted it, indented two spaces, directly above the `try {` that wraps the write loop in `commandApply`, with one blank line after `let writing = null;`. No code changed.\n\nNo other file touched (the test file shows as modified in `git status` from earlier uncommitted lane work; I made no edit to it).\n\n## Verify output\n\n`node --check` → exits 0:\n```\nnode --check exit: 0\n```\n\n`node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs` → `fail 0`:\n```\nℹ tests 43\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 43\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 14881.641666\n```\n\n`rg -n -A1 \"of its own rather than borrowing one the usage already spends on another meaning\"` → comment line, then a line ending `try {`:\n```\n1412:  // of its own rather than borrowing one the usage already spends on another meaning.\n1413-  try {\n```\n\n`rg -n \"^function commandApply\"` → `1343:function commandApply(options, output, hooks) {`, and 1412 > 1343, so the comment now sits inside `commandApply`.\n\nNothing I could not do. The task checkbox in `tasks.md` is left unticked as instructed.","time":{"start":1794562083740,"end":1794562087126}}}
